    "index_image_with_text_baA6PB": {
      "type": "index__image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "image_34wGj9": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/goats_1200x_3b65f5b3-5f3b-4792-9c63-fa93f76c7b9e.webp",
            "mobile_image": "shopify://shop_images/goats_1200x_3b65f5b3-5f3b-4792-9c63-fa93f76c7b9e.webp",
            "image_link": ""
          }
        },
        "text_zpm8Yq": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "title": "",
            "heading_size": "regular",
            "text": "<p><strong>FAMILY LEGACY</strong></p><p>For over a century, the Stevenson family has been at the heart of the woollen industry. It all began with Herbert Stevenson, who ran a woollen mill on the outskirts of Edinburgh, making his own brand of Scottish tweeds. When Drummond joined the business, their Macnab tweeds were sold across Europe and the US.</p><p>Peter Stevenson then introduced cashmere to the mix, traveling to Inner Mongolia over 50 years ago to source the world's finest fibres. Today, we continue to work with the same trusted partners whilst being based in Hong Kong, blending tradition with innovation to create timeless pieces which your kids will love now, and their own children will treasure later.</p>",
            "alignment": "left",
            "vertical_position": "center",
            "button_label": "LEARN MORE",
            "link": "shopify://pages/family-legacy",
            "button_style": "button--primary",
            "background": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "text_color": "rgba(0,0,0,0)",
            "mobile_title": "FAMILY LEGACY",
            "mobile_heading_size": "same_as_desktop",
            "mobile_text": "<p>The Stevensons have been working in the woollen industry for well over a century. It started with Herbert Stevenson who used to run a woollen mill producing his own brand of Scottish tweeds on the outskirts of Edinburgh. When Drummond joined the firm, their brand of Macnab tweeds was sold throughout Europe and the US. Peter then added cashmere to the mix. Peter first went up to Inner Mongolia over 40 years ago and the Stevensons have been working with the same cashmere partners up there ever since.</p>",
            "mobile_alignment": "same_as_desktop"
          }
        }
      },
